{"name":"Maine Coon Orange","hex":"#c2792b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Obsolete form of main."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Obsolete form of main."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maine"},{"term":"coon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A black person.","A raccoon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt raccoons.","To traverse by crawling, as a ledge."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coon"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maine Coon","blocks":[{"text":"The Maine Coon is a large domesticated cat breed. The breed is selectively bred from one of the oldest landraces in North America, and is pedigreed in all major cat registries worldwide. It originated in the U.S. state of Maine, where it is the official state cat. The Maine Coon is a large and social cat, commonly referred to as \"the gentle giant\". The breed is predominantly known for its large size and its long and dense coat of fur which helps it survive in the harsh climate of Maine. The Maine Coon is often cited as having \"dog-like\" characteristics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/M%C3%A2le_Black_Silver_Blotched_Tabby.jpeg/330px-M%C3%A2le_Black_Silver_Blotched_Tabby.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maine_Coon","wikidata":"Q42659"},{"title":"Maine","blocks":[{"text":"Maine is a state in the New England region of the United States, and the northeasternmost state in the contiguous United States. It borders New Hampshire to the west, the Gulf of Maine to the southeast, and the Canadian provinces of New Brunswick and Quebec to the northeast and northwest, and shares a maritime border with Nova Scotia. It is the only state to border only one other state. Maine is the largest state in New England by total area, almost as large as the combined area of the remaining five states. Of the 50 U.S. states, it is the 12th-smallest by area, the 9th-least populous, the 13th-least densely populated, and the most rural. As of 2024, Maine's population stood at a Census-estimated 1,400,000, the state's highest-ever population estimate. Maine's capital is Augusta, while its most populous city is Portland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Flag_of_the_State_of_Maine.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_State_of_Maine.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maine","wikidata":"Q724"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/35/Cosey_the_Maine_Coon_cat%2C_1895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https:/